{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For YHWH knows</b> — There is no doubt that the honored HaShem knows the universals and the particulars. The universals are the soul of every living thing for all creatures, and the particulars are every species and species on its own, or even every single creature on its own, for all are the work of His hands. Only the knowledge of the particular to each one in a general way — whether for the righteous or for the wicked — we have known, and He has always known the known crafts [n]. And because the souls of the righteous endure and persist forever, therefore He knows them; and He also knows that the souls of the wicked perish. Behold, the meaning: for the way of the wicked is to destruction. And if the souls of the wicked perish, all the more so the souls of the scorners; or the word 'wicked' includes sinners and scorners."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the known crafts' (אומנות הנודעות) is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as it stands in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:01.510888002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}